{
  "case_id": "2016-15-457",
  "document_hash": "9037be114ed53f1c2c821c48dfffebfff48f6112690e3f3855ba79e7e9d7b9e4",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Microsoft Corporation",
      "case_id": "2016-15-457",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9037be114ed53f1c2c821c48dfffebfff48f6112690e3f3855ba79e7e9d7b9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9037be114ed5-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Years after Livesay, the rules committee considered what options should be available to plaintiffs who find themselves in precisely the situation the plaintiffs here claim to have found themselves, having class certification denied in a case where they claim the individual claims make it impractical to litigate ahead on an individualized basis. In the system that the rules committee adopted and that this Court endorsed in Rule 23(f) in the system discretionary review, the plaintiff's theory here, with the voluntary dismissal tactic they wish to use, would upend that carefully considered rule."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-15-457",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9037be114ed53f1c2c821c48dfffebfff48f6112690e3f3855ba79e7e9d7b9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9037be114ed5-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument first this morning in case 15-457, Microsoft Corporation v. Baker."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-457",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9037be114ed53f1c2c821c48dfffebfff48f6112690e3f3855ba79e7e9d7b9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9037be114ed5-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: And may I ask, a lot of your briefing in this case operates on the premise that there really was -- that this claim will spring back, that there was some kind of reservation --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-457",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9037be114ed53f1c2c821c48dfffebfff48f6112690e3f3855ba79e7e9d7b9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9037be114ed5-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Mr. Fisher, you've been arguing this in the alternative, but what do you think is the critical fact for you? Is it that they dismissed their claim voluntarily? Is it that they dismissed their claim voluntarily with prejudice? Is it that the case is not moot? What's your best argument and what's your best critical fact that defines the outcome in this case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-15-457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9037be114ed53f1c2c821c48dfffebfff48f6112690e3f3855ba79e7e9d7b9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9037be114ed5-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Well, but -- but as a practical matter, that's not going to happen, right? I mean, they have just their individual claim. It's -- it's worth in Justice Breyer's case 10 cents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-15-457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9037be114ed53f1c2c821c48dfffebfff48f6112690e3f3855ba79e7e9d7b9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9037be114ed5-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: This is a case where there were two Rule 23(f) motions, both denied, and we're talking about the same court of appeals."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-15-457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9037be114ed53f1c2c821c48dfffebfff48f6112690e3f3855ba79e7e9d7b9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9037be114ed5-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Let me ask you, because you mentioned Rule 23. The rule makers went through a lot of work to figure out what to do with an interlocutory ruling on class action status. And it came up with 23(f)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9037be114ed53f1c2c821c48dfffebfff48f6112690e3f3855ba79e7e9d7b9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9037be114ed5-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, what is the circuit split on this?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-15-457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9037be114ed53f1c2c821c48dfffebfff48f6112690e3f3855ba79e7e9d7b9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9037be114ed5-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But what is your best support in any case from this Court for the proposition that a voluntary conditional dismissal with prejudice is a final decision?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stris",
      "case_id": "2016-15-457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9037be114ed53f1c2c821c48dfffebfff48f6112690e3f3855ba79e7e9d7b9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9037be114ed5-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In -- in Procter & Gamble, Your Honor. And in Procter & Gamble, you have a discovery order saying that the United States had to turn over a grand jury transcript."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-15-457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9037be114ed53f1c2c821c48dfffebfff48f6112690e3f3855ba79e7e9d7b9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9037be114ed5-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What about Procter & Gamble, which you -- you've cited a number of times in this argument? But I thought that that decision said a plaintiff who voluntarily dismisses a complaint may not appeal that decision."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2016-15-457",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "9037be114ed53f1c2c821c48dfffebfff48f6112690e3f3855ba79e7e9d7b9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9037be114ed5-0003-0004",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "my friend says that the committee that adopted Rule 23(f) was aware of the circuit split and some courts having allowed this procedure they'd like to go forward with, and that's a rather remarkable statement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-457",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "9037be114ed53f1c2c821c48dfffebfff48f6112690e3f3855ba79e7e9d7b9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9037be114ed5-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: But that's not quite -- that's not quite right. You deny 23(f) and there's a choice -- or no choice. You have to --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2016-15-457",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "9037be114ed53f1c2c821c48dfffebfff48f6112690e3f3855ba79e7e9d7b9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9037be114ed5-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And I'll just read you one sentence from the committee notes. They say: An order denying certification may confront the plaintiff with a"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2016-15-457",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9037be114ed53f1c2c821c48dfffebfff48f6112690e3f3855ba79e7e9d7b9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9037be114ed5-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So the rules committee considered this exact question and thought the only way to get an appeal for sure was to litigate the case ahead."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-15-457",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "9037be114ed53f1c2c821c48dfffebfff48f6112690e3f3855ba79e7e9d7b9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9037be114ed5-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2016-15-457",
